   RowBox[{
   "Print", "[", "\"\<One may check that any of our homogeneous metrics are \
isometric to one in which u=0. Combined with the observation that udot is \
proportional to u, the subspace of metrics defined by u=0 is invariant under \
the Ricci flow. As a consequence, we may without loss of generality assume \
that u=0. Hence, we obtain the following equations:\>\"", "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
